    {
      "id": "landscape-short-height-inspector-is-not-a-first-screen-task",
      "severity": "P1",
      "result": "fail",
      "summary": "VETO. At 667x390, every inspected scene shows only the verdict and horizontal object rail above the fixed tab bar; the selected inspector, its evidence and its action are below the fold. At 844x390, the width-based split inspector appears, but the header, verdict and fixed tab bar still leave only a narrow, cut-off strip of its content. A landscape patrol therefore starts with a selection affordance instead of an inspectable operational object, which breaks the required three-second hierarchy and reduces iKuai-style status density.",
      "evidence": [
        "_acceptance/mobile-telemetry-runtime/single-landscape667-overview.png",
        "_acceptance/mobile-telemetry-runtime/all-offline-landscape667-overview.png",
        "_acceptance/mobile-telemetry-runtime/no-snapshot-landscape667-overview.png",
